  "findings": [
    "No waiting, requested, or action_required runs were returned. PR81 and PR82 pending_deployments endpoints each returned an empty array. The inspected CI workflow declares no job environment approval gate.",
    "Main CI run 44262124202 at 28ed7166 has eight successful jobs and its macOS Intel race job still running; latest main CI run 44265254428 at cdc8112c is pending with no instantiated jobs. Their shared workflow concurrency group explains the latter main-run wait.",
    "PR81 has its own group and five successful jobs, including both native jobs and three Linux jobs; four Linux jobs remain queued. PR82 has its own group and all seven configured Linux jobs queued. The main concurrency group does not by itself explain those distinct PR queues.",
    "Across the observed instantiated job rows, 40 are queued and one is running. Twenty-eight queued jobs belong to four other PR runs, seven to PR82, four to PR81, and one to scorecard. No repository Linux job was reported in_progress in this snapshot.",
    "No account/organization concurrency metrics, billing diagnostics, or runner-availability explanation were exposed by these observations. Runner capacity or billing cannot be asserted as the cause.",
    "cancel-in-progress:false protects a currently running main workflow. With no queue property, the documented default still permits only one pending run; a later pending run replaces an earlier pending run. Thus the workflow comment that every back-to-back main push keeps a cross-OS run overstates the configuration."
